{
  "_comment": [
    "The atriumd service definition: what peinit starts, and how.",
    "",
    "Identity is SYSTEM because atriumd originates logons: /run/logon.sock",
    "admits SYSTEM alone, and authd's may_originate is SYSTEM-only until its",
    "per-caller policy table exists. It is the ONLY privileged process in",
    "Atrium -- it spawns atrium-server, the half that touches the network,",
    "under a copy of its own token with every privilege deleted, and the two",
    "share one socketpair. Nothing listening on a port runs as SYSTEM.",
    "",
    "Requires lpsd, as login-console does: authd being up means a prompt can",
    "be COLLECTED; lpsd being registered means it can be ANSWERED, and lpsd",
    "itself depends on authd, so this one edge orders the whole chain.",
    "",
    "Readiness is Notify (0): atriumd sends READY=1 once atrium-server is",
    "spawned. The listener is the server's, so a bind failure shows as the",
    "server exiting and atriumd following it.",
    "",
    "RestartPolicy is Always (2): sessions do not survive an atriumd restart",
    "(by decision, for now), so a restart is the recovery for everything.",
    "",
    "Shipped by the atriumd package into /usr/share/regim/; inert until an",
    "image names it in [registry] autoapply."
  ],
  "keys": [
    { "path": "Machine\\System" },
    { "path": "Machine\\System\\Services" },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Services\\atriumd",
      "values": [
        { "name": "ImagePath", "type": "sz", "data": "/usr/sbin/atriumd" },
        { "name": "Triggers", "type": "multi", "data": ["boot"] },
        { "name": "Requires", "type": "multi", "data": ["lpsd"] },
        { "name": "Identity", "type": "sz", "data": "SYSTEM" },
        { "name": "Readiness", "type": "dword", "data": 0 },
        { "name": "RestartPolicy", "type": "dword", "data": 2 },
        { "name": "ErrorControl", "type": "dword", "data": 0 },
        { "name": "DisplayName", "type": "sz", "data": "Atrium web session host" },
        { "name": "Description", "type": "sz", "data": "The Peios web UI: logs users on through the authority and serves the browser-delivered session on port 8080" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
